\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces (a) The materialization--completion bottleneck shift and the interior optimum of conditional (success-only) time-to-success at $K^\star {=}8$, measured on the $35{,}640$-run peer-broadcast sweep of the companion Q/R/M/C study~\citep  {songlines1}: $P(M^\star |R^\star )$ falls and $P(C^\star |M^\star )$ rises with $K$, while mean $t_{\mathrm  {succ}}$ has an interior minimum. (b) The measured CSM sweep over cadence $K$ and trust threshold $\tau $: mean $t_{\mathrm  {succ}}$ is essentially $\tau $-invariant and only weakly $K$-dependent, and mission success is flat in $(K,\tau )$ (range $0.015$). The trust threshold is \emph  {not} the active lever in this regime --- the interior operating point is the cadence effect of panel (a), not a two-dimensional optimum island.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{p4:fig:ktrust}{{2}{5}{(a) The materialization--completion bottleneck shift and the interior optimum of conditional (success-only) time-to-success at $K^\star {=}8$, measured on the $35{,}640$-run peer-broadcast sweep of the companion Q/R/M/C study~\citep {songlines1}: $P(M^\star |R^\star )$ falls and $P(C^\star |M^\star )$ rises with $K$, while mean $t_{\mathrm {succ}}$ has an interior minimum. (b) The measured CSM sweep over cadence $K$ and trust threshold $\tau $: mean $t_{\mathrm {succ}}$ is essentially $\tau $-invariant and only weakly $K$-dependent, and mission success is flat in $(K,\tau )$ (range $0.015$). The trust threshold is \emph {not} the active lever in this regime --- the interior operating point is the cadence effect of panel (a), not a two-dimensional optimum island}{figure.2}{}}
